{"t": 1794111656.3893335, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "CI note: the `contract-tests` check was failing on `fee(2.675) == 2.68` (actual: 2.67).\n\nRoot cause: binary floats can't represent 2.675 exactly (it is stored as 2.6749999999999998...), so `round()` rounded the tie down. That violates the card-network rounding contract in PAY-88, which requires fees to be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents.\n\nWhat I changed in `payments/fees.py` (pushed to `fees-float`):\n- Compute the fee from `Decimal(str(amount))` instead of float arithmetic, so the decimal value the caller passed in is preserved exactly.\n- Quantize to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n- Convert back to `float` so the function signature and return type are unchanged.\n\nThe existing formula (`amount * 0.01 * 100`) is untouched; only the rounding is now exact. `fee(2.675)` now returns 2.68, `fee(1.005)` returns 1.01, and `fee(100.0)` still returns 100.0.\n\nVerified locally: `python -m pytest -q` passes, and I checked the contract cases directly.\n\nHeads-up: switching this calculation to floats can't satisfy PAY-88 - float rounding at half-cent boundaries is inherently unreliable, so the Decimal path is required for this contract.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
